use std
into layout.amni
lang amni
Amni-Drive's area-maximizing, concave-arc hugging cockpit layout and driver-ergonomic button-placement engine. Critical interactive content (Map, Media, Voice/Nav buttons) is primary and occupies the full display; secondary telemetry (Speed, Weather icon + temp, Clock) tucks cleanly into natural spandrel gaps or sidebar headers without wasting dedicated widget columns. All coordinates and sizes are 32-bit floats in logical pixels.
Struct `Rect` holds `x`, `y`, `w`, and `h` as 32-bit floats.
Struct `Circle` holds `cx`, `cy`, and `r` as 32-bit floats.
Struct `HitButton` holds `id` as a 32-bit integer, `rect` as a `Rect`, and `primary` as a boolean.
Struct `Pod` holds `kind` as a 32-bit integer (0 map, 1 media, 2 speed_badge, 3 weather_badge, 4 apps_badge, 5 clock_badge), `shape` as a 32-bit integer (0 rect, 1 circle, 2 hex, 3 capsule, 4 crescent_left, 5 crescent_right, 6 crescent_bottom), `rect` as a `Rect`, `circle` as a `Circle`, `cutout` as a `Circle` (concentric map circle carved out of concave crescent wings when `cutout.r > 0`), `safe_rect` as a `Rect`, and `chamfer` as a 32-bit float.
Struct `CockpitPlan` holds `screen_w` and `screen_h` as 32-bit floats, `layout_id` as a 32-bit integer, `dock_rect` as a `Rect`, `stage_rect` as a `Rect`, `portrait` as a boolean, `dock_bottom` as a boolean, `buttons` as a growable list of `HitButton`, and `pods` as a growable list of `Pod`.
Function `make_rect` takes `x`, `y`, `w`, and `h` as 32-bit floats and returns a `Rect`.
Function `rects_overlap` takes two `Rect` values `a` and `b` and returns true if their interiors strictly overlap by more than 0.5 pixels on both axes.
Function `rect_inside` takes `inner` and `outer` as `Rect` values and returns true if `inner` lies inside `outer` within 0.5 pixel tolerance on all four edges and has positive width and height.
Function `inscribe_circle` takes a `Rect` `r` and returns a `Circle` centered in `r` with radius equal to half of the smaller of `r.w` and `r.h`.
Function `circle_safe_rect` takes a `Circle` `c` and returns the chord-safe inner `Rect` centered at `c.cx`, `c.cy` with width and height equal to `c.r * 1.4142`.
Function `make_pod` takes `kind` and `shape` as 32-bit integers, `r` as a `Rect`, and `cutout` as a `Circle`, returning a `Pod`. When `shape` is 1 (circle), set `circle` to `inscribe_circle` of `r`, `safe_rect` to `circle_safe_rect` of that circle, and `chamfer` to 0. When `shape` is 2 (hex), set `chamfer` to `min(r.w, r.h) * 0.075` clamped between 12 and 26, and inset `safe_rect` by `chamfer * 0.5` on all sides. When `shape` is 3 (capsule), set `chamfer` to `min(min(r.w, r.h) * 0.28, 48.0)` and inset `safe_rect` horizontally by `min(r.w * 0.07, chamfer * 0.5)` and vertically by 8. When `shape` is 4 (crescent_left) or 5 (crescent_right) or 6 (crescent_bottom), set `chamfer` to 24.0 and `safe_rect` to `r` inset by 8 pixels. Otherwise (rect), `safe_rect` equals `r` and `chamfer` is 0.
Function `compute_cockpit` takes `screen_w`, `screen_h`, `min_hit`, `gutter`, and `pad` as 32-bit floats, `layout_id` as a 32-bit integer (0 twin chrono, 1 solar binnacle, 2 orb center, 3 horizon dials, 4 hex cockpit, 5 capsule deck, 6 asym triptych, 7 tri cockpit, 8 split, 9 full map), `dock_mode` as a 32-bit integer (0 auto driver rail, 1 bottom dock, 2 right-hand-drive rail), and `swap_map_media` as a boolean, returning a `CockpitPlan`.
First decide orientation: `portrait` is true when `screen_h` is greater than `screen_w * 1.05`. `dock_bottom` is true when `portrait` is true or `dock_mode` is 1.
Compute the slim, high-efficiency driver dock and stage rectangles:
- When `dock_bottom` is true: `dock_h` is `max(min_hit + 10.0, 68.0)` clamped to at most `screen_h * 0.16`. `dock_rect` sits along the bottom edge `(pad, screen_h - dock_h - pad, screen_w - 2.0 * pad, dock_h)`. `stage_rect` fills `(pad, pad, screen_w - 2.0 * pad, screen_h - dock_h - 2.0 * pad - gutter)`.
- When `dock_bottom` is false: `dock_w` is `max(min_hit + 12.0, 72.0)` clamped to at most `screen_w * 0.125`. If `dock_mode` is 2 (right-hand drive), `dock_rect` sits on the right edge `(screen_w - dock_w - pad, pad, dock_w, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)` and `stage_rect` fills `(pad, pad, screen_w - dock_w - 2.0 * pad - gutter, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)`. Otherwise (left-hand drive default), `dock_rect` sits on the left edge `(pad, pad, dock_w, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)` and `stage_rect` fills `(pad + dock_w + gutter, pad, screen_w - dock_w - 2.0 * pad - gutter, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)`.
Place the six driver-priority buttons inside `dock_rect` with ids 1 (NAV), 2 (MEDIA), 3 (APPS), 4 (VOICE, marked primary true), 5 (VIEW), and 6 (SET):
- Along the dock's long axis, divide the available span (`long_span - 5.0 * btn_gap`) into 6 equal slots where `btn_gap` is `max(gutter * 0.65, 7.0)` reduced only if needed so every slot stays at least `min_hit * 0.85` (and never below 48 pixels). Each button fills its slot along the long axis and the full cross-axis of `dock_rect` inset by 3 pixels on each side.
Next, place the primary interactive pods and compact secondary spandrel badges inside `stage_rect` (`sx = stage_rect.x`, `sy = stage_rect.y`, `sw = stage_rect.w`, `sh = stage_rect.h`, `g = gutter`). Let `zero_c` be a zero `Circle`. Let `k_left` be 1 if `swap_map_media` else 0, and `k_right` be 0 if `swap_map_media` else 1.
- Layout 0 (`TWIN_CHRONO`): Maximized dual circular dials filling full height with secondary badges nestled neatly in the top and bottom V-shaped spandrel valleys between the two circles.
  - If `portrait`: top circular pod (`k_left`, 49 percent of `sh - g`), bottom circular pod (`k_right`, 49 percent of `sh - g`), plus compact top-left `speed_badge` (width 94, height 44, capsule) and top-right `weather_badge` (width 94, height 44, capsule) tucked cleanly into the vacant upper corners of `stage_rect`.
  - If landscape: compute `dial_d = min(sh, (sw - g) * 0.50)`. Place left circular pod (`k_left`, square `dial_d` by `dial_d` vertically centered at `sx` on left) and right circular pod (`k_right`, square `dial_d` by `dial_d` vertically centered at `sx + sw - dial_d` on right). In the natural top V-gap between the two circles, place a centered capsule `speed_badge` (width `clamp(sw * 0.22, 112.0, 176.0)`, height `clamp(sh * 0.13, 44.0, 64.0)`) at `sy + 4`. In the natural bottom V-gap between the two circles, place a centered capsule `weather_badge` (width `clamp(sw * 0.22, 112.0, 176.0)`, height `clamp(sh * 0.13, 44.0, 64.0)`) at `sy + sh - bh - 4`.
- Layout 1 (`SOLAR_BINNACLE`): Giant centered circular map (`96%` of stage height) hugged seamlessly by concave-arc crescent wings on BOTH left and right — zero wasted corners!
  - If `portrait`: giant top circular `map` (`dial_d = min(sw, sh * 0.56)` centered horizontally at `sy`), concave-top `crescent_bottom` `media` wing below it overlapping up into the lower corners of the map's bounding box (`y = sy + dial_d * 0.80`, height remaining to `sy + sh`) with `cutout` equal to the map circle expanded in radius by `g`, plus compact `speed_badge` (top-left spandrel, 96 by 46 capsule) and `weather_badge` (top-right spandrel, 96 by 46 capsule).
  - If landscape: `map_d = min(sh * 0.96, sw * 0.54)`. Place giant circular `map` centered in `stage_rect` (`cx = sx + sw * 0.45`, `cy = sy + sh * 0.5`, radius `map_r = map_d * 0.5`, clamping `cx` so the circle stays inside `stage_rect`). Define `cut = Circle(cx, cy, map_r + g)`. On the left side (`x = sx`, width `max(120.0, cx - sx - map_r * 0.42)`), place a `crescent_left` pod (`kind = 2` speed/telemetry + quick controls) that hugs the left curve of the map using `cut`. On the right side (`x = cx + map_r * 0.42`, width `sx + sw - x`), place a HUGE `crescent_right` interactive `media` pod (`kind = 1`) that hugs the right curve of the map using `cut`, giving Spotify/Media full height and generous width! Tuck a compact `weather_badge` capsule (`w = 112, h = 44`) cleanly into the top-left corner (`sx + 6, sy + 6`) and a compact `clock_badge` capsule (`w = 112, h = 44`) into the bottom-left corner (`sx + 6, sy + sh - 50`).
- Layout 2 (`ORB_CENTER`): Same giant circular map orb (`map_d = min(sh * 0.94, sw * 0.56)` anchored left-of-center) with a single sweeping `crescent_right` interactive `media` wing hugging its right curve (`cutout = map_r + g`) and compact `speed_badge` + `weather_badge` pills tucked into the top-left and bottom-left vacant corners of the circle!
- Layout 3 (`HORIZON_DIALS`): Full-bleed rectangular `map` filling `stage_rect`, with compact floating `speed_badge` + `weather_badge` pills top-left and a floating circular `media` orb bottom-right (`clamp(min(sw, sh) * 0.40, 128.0, 210.0)`).
- Layout 4 (`HEX_COCKPIT`): Zero passive widget column! Two bold chamfered octagonal interactive pods filling 100 percent of `stage_rect`: `k_left` (`60%` of `sw - g`) and `k_right` (`40%` of `sw - g`) in landscape (or `58%` over `42%` in portrait), plus compact `speed_badge` and `weather_badge` pills nestled cleanly in the top-right header area of the map pod's bevel!
- Layout 5 (`CAPSULE_DECK`): Sleek architectural rounded pods (`shape = 3`, radius clamped to at most 48px): if `portrait`, `map` (`62%` height) over full-width interactive `media` (`38%` height), with compact `speed_badge` + `weather_badge` pills tucked into the top corners of the map; if landscape, `map` (`60%` width) beside interactive `media` (`40%` width) with compact top-right `speed_badge` + `weather_badge` corner chips.
- Layout 6 (`ASYM_TRIPTYCH`): Golden-ratio interactive split (`62%` `k_left`, `38%` `k_right`, both `shape = 0`) with compact `speed_badge` and `weather_badge` corner pills instead of a third passive column.
- Layout 7 (`TRI_COCKPIT`): `k_left` (`58%`) and `k_right` (`42%`) with compact `speed_badge` + `weather_badge` overlay chips.
- Layout 8 (`SPLIT`): 55 percent `k_left` and 45 percent `k_right` (both rect).
- Layout 9 (`FULL_MAP`, or any other value): Single rectangular `map` pod filling `stage_rect` plus compact top-right `speed_badge` and `weather_badge` chips.
Function `validate_cockpit` takes a `CockpitPlan` and returns 0 if every button is inside `dock_rect`, no two buttons overlap, every button has width and height at least 48 pixels, `dock_rect` and `stage_rect` do not overlap, and every pod's `rect` lies inside `stage_rect`; otherwise return a nonzero error code (1 button out of dock, 2 buttons overlap, 3 button too small, 4 dock overlaps stage, 5 pod out of stage).
